# Every text file is stored with LF in the repo, whatever the contributor's OS.
# Without this, a Windows commit can rewrite every line ending of a file and the
# pull request shows the whole file as changed, which also breeds merge
# conflicts. It also keeps shell scripts runnable inside the Linux container.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Input CSVs (fixtures, rubric scores) are kept byte for byte as they were
# saved. Some hold CRLF or mixed endings, partly inside quoted cells, and
# converting them would change cell contents. This rule must stay below the one
# above: the later match wins.
data/**/*.csv -text
